# Git must store and check out every file byte for byte.
#
# 221 research files are frozen by SHA-256 manifests (docs/*_freeze.sha256). They use LF, CRLF
# and mixed line endings, so any line-ending normalisation, working-tree re-encoding, ident
# expansion or content filter would break their hashes on checkout. The first rule therefore
# unsets every converting attribute for all paths, whatever core.autocrlf or core.eol is set to.
# No later rule may set text, eol, filter, ident or working-tree-encoding
# (enforced by python -m tools.release check).
* -text -eol -filter -ident -working-tree-encoding

# Binary images: no textual diff or merge.
*.png binary

# The generated release inventory is shown collapsed in GitHub diffs. Lock files and freeze
# manifests stay expanded so that changes to them are reviewed.
docs/release_inventory.csv linguist-generated
